      "hints": [
        "Differentiate $y = 2x^{3/2} - 3x - 4x^{1/2} + 4$ to get $\\frac{dy}{dx} = 3\\sqrt{x} - 3 - \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{x}}$.",
        "Evaluate at $x = 4$: $\\frac{dy}{dx} = 3(2) - 3 - 1 = 2$.",
        "Form tangent equation at $(4, 0)$: $y = 2x - 8$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Differentiate the curve equation term by term with respect to $x$:\n$$\\frac{dy}{dx} = 2\\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\right)x^{\\frac{1}{2}} - 3 - 4\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)x^{-\\frac{1}{2}} = 3x^{\\frac{1}{2}} - 3 - 2x^{-\\frac{1}{2}} = 3\\sqrt{x} - 3 - \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{x}}$$",
        "Evaluate the gradient at the given point $(4, 0)$:\n$$m_T = \\left.\\frac{dy}{dx}\\right|_{x=4} = 3\\sqrt{4} - 3 - \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{4}} = 3(2) - 3 - \\frac{2}{2} = 6 - 3 - 1 = 2$$",
        "Write the equation of the tangent line at $(4, 0)$:\n$$y - 0 = 2(x - 4) \\implies y = 2x - 8$$"
      ],
